{
  "$comment": "Single media manifest. Paths are relative to `base`. Character clips are stacked-alpha (colour top half, alpha as luma bottom half); `premultiplied` says whether the colour half is premultiplied by alpha. otto/vee.clips hold the silent idle loops (and the /frames/thanks pop). `lines` are the 8 fixed talking lines: one clip per line with its own audio track baked in (AV1+Opus, HEVC+AAC) and <id>.words.json word timings, so lips, sound and captions share one clock. A line with `pending` has no clip yet: the character stays on the idle loop and the line shows as a plain caption. `node scripts/lines-import.mjs <keyed_dir>` encodes delivered clips and fills the entries. Film order = ring order: films without `ring: false` orbit Otto on the first screen (product-first posters lead; at most 2 character faces; Red Light is the featured film). `ring: false` films (VESPER Keep the Light, SOL, Otto) show on /work and in the home Work grid only.",
